  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe root cause of the vulnerability is a flawed order of operations within the `GrowthHYBR` contract's `deposit()` function. The function first increases the vault's total assets by locking the new user's deposit into the `veNFT`, and only afterward does it calculate the number of shares the user should receive. This causes the depositor's own funds to be included in the `totalAssets` denominator of the share price calculation, severely and unfairly reducing the number of shares they are minted.\n\n**The execution flow is as follows:**\n\nA user deposits `amount`. The contract first calls `IVotingEscrow.deposit_for()`, which adds `amount` to the locked assets. It then calls `calculateShares(amount)`, which uses the now-inflated `totalAssets` value. This results in the formula `shares = amount * old_totalSupply / (old_totalAssets + amount)`, penalizing the depositor.\n\n```solidity\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient) external nonReentrant {\n    require(amount > 0, \"Zero amount\");\n    recipient = recipient == address(0) ? msg.sender : recipient;\n    \n    IERC20(HYBR).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    \n    if (veTokenId == 0) {\n        _initializeVeNFT(amount);\n    } else {\n(1)@>    IERC20(HYBR).approve(votingEscrow, amount);\n(2)@>    IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).deposit_for(veTokenId, amount);\n\n        _extendLockToMax();\n    }\n    \n(3)@> uint256 shares = calculateShares(amount);\n    \n    _mint(recipient, shares);\n    \n    _addTransferLock(recipient, shares);\n    \n    emit Deposit(msg.sender, amount, shares);\n}\n```\n\nThe impacts of this vulnerability are critical:\n\n1.  Any user depositing after the first will receive significantly fewer shares than they are entitled to, resulting in an immediate and permanent loss of principal.\n2.  A malicious first depositor can deposit a minimal amount (e.g., 1 wei) to manipulate the share price. This causes the next depositor, regardless of their deposit size (e.g., 1000 HYBR), to receive zero shares due to integer division, leading to a total loss of their funds.\n3.  The contract's core economic function is broken. Instead of a fair yield-bearing vault, it acts as a predatory mechanism that benefits the first depositor at the expense of all subsequent users.\n4.  This flaw renders the `GrowthHYBR` contract unusable and poses a critical risk of asset loss to its users.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nThe order of operations in the `deposit()` function must be reversed. The contract must first calculate the shares to be minted based on the state of the vault *before* the new deposit is added. After the shares have been calculated and minted, the new deposit can then be added to the locked assets in the `veNFT`. This ensures a fair share price calculation for every depositor.\n\n```diff\nfunction deposit(uint256 amount, address recipient) external nonReentrant {\n    require(amount > 0, \"Zero amount\");\n    recipient = recipient == address(0) ? msg.sender : recipient;\n    \n    IERC20(HYBR).transferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), amount);\n    \n-   if (veTokenId == 0) {\n-       _initializeVeNFT(amount);\n-   } else {\n-       IERC20(HYBR).approve(votingEscrow, amount);\n-       IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).deposit_for(veTokenId, amount);\n-\n-       _extendLockToMax();\n-   }\n-   \n-   uint256 shares = calculateShares(amount);\n+   uint256 shares = calculateShares(amount);\n+\n+   if (veTokenId == 0) {\n+       _initializeVeNFT(amount);\n+   } else {\n+       IERC20(HYBR).approve(votingEscrow, amount);\n+       IVotingEscrow(votingEscrow).deposit_for(veTokenId, amount);\n+\n+       _extendLockToMax();\n+   }\n    \n    _mint(recipient, shares);\n    \n    _addTransferLock(recipient, shares);\n    \n    emit Deposit(msg.sender, amount, shares);\n}\n```",
